The `new Map.Entry[values().length]` creates a raw-type array, requiring `@SuppressWarnings({ "unchecked", "rawtypes" })`. A slightly cleaner alternative that avoids the raw type entirely would be to use a `List`:
```java
static Map<String, LinkComponents> readLinksBySymbol(InputStream inputStream) throws IOException {
    final var entries = new ArrayList<Map.Entry<String, LinkComponents>>(values().length);
    createLinkComponentEntries(inputStream, entries);
    return Map.ofEntries(entries);
}
```
This eliminates the need for the suppression annotation and the `Map.Entry<?, ?>[]` parameter type on the helper method. Minor, but it keeps the code free of raw types.

